    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d319">

                <pb facs="0452" n="384" sameAs="frus:frus1867p1/pg384"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr. Fox</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1867-02-25"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >February</hi> 25, 1867</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have received your interesting letter of
                    this date, giving an account of the manner in which you have executed the
                    instructions of this department with reference to the presentation to the
                    Emperor of Russia of the resolution of Congress congratulating him upon his
                    escape from an attempted assassination. In reply, I have to inform you that your
                    proceedings upon the occasion referred to are entirely approved.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p> G. V. Fox, Esq.</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
